s=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the Kimball County record runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids February to March and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 39 years. In 2025 the county&rsquo;s middle value saw October to November at 38% and November to December at 32% of normal. So far in 2026, March to April sat at 26% and June to July at 80% on the county&rsquo;s middle value. Grid 25605 had its driest year in 2012 at 47%.</p>"}
